# Editorial annotations only; OWL axioms and SHACL constraints above are unchanged.
@prefix dlv: <https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .

<https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv> skos:scopeNote "Use in declarations of physical multi-dimensional storage. Logical axis meaning is distinct from byte strides, chunk order and encoded payload interpretation."@en .
dlv:Axis skos:definition "The logical meaning of a dimension, independent of the dimension's extent or storage stride."@en .
dlv:CellDataTypeRuleShape rdfs:label "Cell Data Type Rule Shape"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv> ;
    skos:definition "Applies to instances of dlv:CellDataTypeRule. bddo:condition takes exactly one value, a HEL expression (an xsd:string or bddo:HelExpression literal). dlv:ruleCellDataType takes exactly one value, an instance of bddo:DataType."@en .
dlv:ChunkedLayoutShape rdfs:label "Chunked Layout Shape"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv> ;
    skos:definition "Applies to instances of dlv:DataLayout. dlv:chunkLengthsFromField takes at most one value; each is an instance of bddo:Field. dlv:chunkOffsetBase takes at most one value; each is one of bddo:streamStart, bddo:streamEnd, bddo:parentStart or bddo:currentPosition. dlv:chunkOffsetsFromField takes at most one value; each is an instance of bddo:Field. dlv:chunkOrder takes at most one value; each is an instance of dlv:ChunkOrder. A chunked dlv:DataLayout (any Dimension declaring dlv:chunkSize, dlv:chunkSizeFromField or dlv:chunkSizeFromExpression) must declare dlv:chunkOffsetsFromField."@en .
dlv:DataLayout skos:definition "A declaration of how logical array cells are addressed in a physical byte region, including dimensions, strides, cell type and optional chunking."@en .
dlv:DataLayoutShape rdfs:label "Data Layout Shape"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv> ;
    skos:definition "Applies to instances of dlv:DataLayout. A dlv:DataLayout fixes its cell type (dlv:cellDataType) or chooses it (dlv:hasConditionalCellDataType), and fixes its dimension order (dlv:hasDimension) or chooses it (dlv:hasConditionalDimensionOrder): one of each pair, never both and never neither. Each focus node is exactly one of these: states dlv:cellDataType and no dlv:hasConditionalCellDataType; states dlv:hasConditionalCellDataType and no dlv:cellDataType and exactly one of these: states dlv:hasDimension and no dlv:hasConditionalDimensionOrder; states dlv:hasConditionalDimensionOrder and no dlv:hasDimension. dlv:cellBitWidth takes at most one value; each is an integer (of any XSD integer datatype) greater than 0. dlv:cellBitWidthFromExpression takes at most one value; each is a HEL expression (an xsd:string or bddo:HelExpression literal). dlv:cellBitWidthFromField takes at most one value; each is an instance of bddo:Field. dlv:cellDataType takes at most one value; each is an instance of bddo:DataType. dlv:cellPackingOrder takes at most one value; each is either bddo:MSBFirst or bddo:LSBFirst. dlv:hasConditionalCellDataType takes at most one value; each is a resource (an IRI or a blank node). dlv:hasConditionalDimensionOrder takes at most one value; each is a resource (an IRI or a blank node). dlv:hasDimension takes at most one value; each is a resource (an IRI or a blank node). Each member of the dlv:hasDimension list is an instance of dlv:Dimension. Every member of a hasConditionalCellDataType list must be a dlv:CellDataTypeRule. Every member of a hasConditionalDimensionOrder list must be a dlv:DimensionOrderRule. A dlv:DataLayout must use at most one packed-width mechanism (cellBitWidth / cellBitWidthFromField / cellBitWidthFromExpression). dlv:cellPackingOrder is only meaningful with dlv:cellBitWidth, dlv:cellBitWidthFromField or dlv:cellBitWidthFromExpression."@en .
dlv:Dimension skos:definition "One position in a data layout's ordered dimensions, with an extent, optional stride or chunk size, and optional axis meaning."@en .
dlv:DimensionOrderRuleShape rdfs:label "Dimension Order Rule Shape"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv> ;
    skos:definition "Applies to instances of dlv:DimensionOrderRule. bddo:condition takes exactly one value, a HEL expression (an xsd:string or bddo:HelExpression literal). dlv:ruleDimensionOrder takes exactly one value, a resource (an IRI or a blank node). Every member of a ruleDimensionOrder list must be a dlv:Dimension."@en .
dlv:DimensionShape rdfs:label "Dimension Shape"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv> ;
    skos:definition "Applies to instances of dlv:Dimension. A dlv:Dimension states its extent exactly one way (dlv:dimensionSize, dlv:dimensionSizeFromField or dlv:dimensionSizeFromExpression) and its chunk extent at most one way (dlv:chunkSize, dlv:chunkSizeFromField or dlv:chunkSizeFromExpression). Each focus node is exactly one of these: states dlv:dimensionSize (an integer (of any XSD integer datatype)), no dlv:dimensionSizeFromField and no dlv:dimensionSizeFromExpression; states dlv:dimensionSizeFromField, no dlv:dimensionSize and no dlv:dimensionSizeFromExpression; states dlv:dimensionSizeFromExpression, no dlv:dimensionSize and no dlv:dimensionSizeFromField and exactly one of these: states no dlv:chunkSize, no dlv:chunkSizeFromField and no dlv:chunkSizeFromExpression; states dlv:chunkSize (an integer (of any XSD integer datatype)), no dlv:chunkSizeFromField and no dlv:chunkSizeFromExpression; states dlv:chunkSizeFromField, no dlv:chunkSize and no dlv:chunkSizeFromExpression; states dlv:chunkSizeFromExpression, no dlv:chunkSize and no dlv:chunkSizeFromField. dlv:chunkSize takes at most one value; each is an integer (of any XSD integer datatype) greater than 0. dlv:chunkSizeFromExpression takes at most one value; each is a HEL expression (an xsd:string or bddo:HelExpression literal). dlv:chunkSizeFromField takes at most one value; each is an instance of bddo:Field. dlv:dimensionSize takes at most one value; each is an integer (of any XSD integer datatype) greater than 0. dlv:dimensionSizeFromExpression takes at most one value; each is a HEL expression (an xsd:string or bddo:HelExpression literal). dlv:dimensionSizeFromField takes at most one value; each is an instance of bddo:Field. dlv:dimensionStride takes at most one value; each is an integer (of any XSD integer datatype) greater than 0. dlv:dimensionStrideFromExpression takes at most one value; each is a HEL expression (an xsd:string or bddo:HelExpression literal). dlv:dimensionStrideFromField takes at most one value; each is an instance of bddo:Field. dlv:hasAxis takes exactly one value, an IRI naming an instance of dlv:Axis. A dlv:Dimension must use at most one stride mechanism (dimensionStride / dimensionStrideFromField / dimensionStrideFromExpression)."@en .
dlv:IntegerValueShape skos:definition "Applied through references from other shapes. An integer value is a literal of an XSD integer-family datatype (xsd:integer, xsd:positiveInteger, xsd:nonNegativeInteger, xsd:int, xsd:long, xsd:unsignedInt, xsd:unsignedLong, xsd:short, xsd:unsignedShort, xsd:byte or xsd:unsignedByte). A conforming value is an integer (of any XSD integer datatype)."@en .
dlv:RangeDatatypeShape skos:definition "Applies to subjects using dlv:cellBitWidth, dlv:cellBitWidthFromExpression, dlv:chunkSize, dlv:chunkSizeFromExpression, dlv:dimensionSize, dlv:dimensionSizeFromExpression, dlv:dimensionStride, dlv:dimensionStrideFromExpression. dlv:cellBitWidth takes a positive integer (rdfs:range xsd:positiveInteger). dlv:cellBitWidthFromExpression takes a HEL expression, an xsd:string or bddo:HelExpression literal (rdfs:range xsd:string). dlv:chunkSize takes a positive integer (rdfs:range xsd:positiveInteger). dlv:chunkSizeFromExpression takes a HEL expression, an xsd:string or bddo:HelExpression literal (rdfs:range xsd:string). dlv:dimensionSize takes a positive integer (rdfs:range xsd:positiveInteger). dlv:dimensionSizeFromExpression takes a HEL expression, an xsd:string or bddo:HelExpression literal (rdfs:range xsd:string). dlv:dimensionStride takes a positive integer (rdfs:range xsd:positiveInteger). dlv:dimensionStrideFromExpression takes a HEL expression, an xsd:string or bddo:HelExpression literal (rdfs:range xsd:string)."@en .
dlv:_prefixes rdfs:label "prefixes"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv> ;
    skos:definition "Namespace prefix declarations reused by SHACL SPARQL constraints and rules. This is validation infrastructure, not a property of parsed data."@en .
dlv:axisBand rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv> ;
    skos:definition "The axis indexing separate bands or channels of a multi-component array."@en .
dlv:axisTime rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv> ;
    skos:definition "The temporal axis of a layout; sample spacing and time reference must be described separately."@en .
dlv:axisX rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv> ;
    skos:definition "The logical horizontal or first spatial coordinate axis of a layout."@en .
dlv:axisY rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv> ;
    skos:definition "The logical vertical-in-grid or second spatial coordinate axis of a layout; ground-coordinate direction is specified separately."@en .
dlv:axisZ rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv> ;
    skos:definition "The third spatial coordinate axis of a layout."@en .
dlv:cellDataType skos:definition "The datatype of a single array cell before any conditional cell-type rule is applied."@en .
dlv:chunkSizeFromField skos:definition "The field whose parsed value supplies the number of cells per chunk along a dimension."@en .
dlv:columnMajor rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv> ;
    skos:definition "Chunk enumeration convention in which the first logical dimension varies fastest."@en .
dlv:dimensionSize skos:definition "The fixed number of cells along a physical-layout dimension."@en .
dlv:dimensionSizeFromField skos:definition "The field whose parsed value supplies a layout dimension's extent."@en .
dlv:hasAxis skos:definition "The logical axis assigned to a physical-layout dimension; it does not itself establish byte order."@en .
dlv:hilbert rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv> ;
    skos:definition "Chunk traversal following a Hilbert space-filling order; the profile/processor must identify the applicable dimension and boundary convention."@en .
dlv:morton rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv> ;
    skos:definition "Chunk traversal ordered by interleaving coordinate bits into a Morton or Z-order key; the profile/processor must agree on dimensionality and bounds."@en .
dlv:rowMajor rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://hexplain.io/ns/dlv> ;
    skos:definition "Chunk enumeration convention in which the last logical dimension varies fastest."@en .
dlv:ruleCellDataType skos:definition "The cell datatype selected when the associated conditional rule matches."@en .
